# Project structure

This repo is After Effects MCP: an AEGP bridge plugin, an MCP server for Claude Code, and one CEP status panel. See `ARCHITECTURE.md` for details.

```
aegp/        AE MCP Bridge (C++, After Effects SDK) — build.sh, test/run.sh
engine/      engine.jsx (ExtendScript ES3) + vocabulary.js (op schema/catalog)
mcp/         server.js (protocol, bridge connection) + tools.js (hot-reloadable tools)
panel/       CEP panel "AE MCP" — index.html, app.js, panel.jsx
shared/      bridge-client.js (used by mcp + panel), CSInterface.js (downloaded, not committed)
CSXS/        manifest.xml — single extension com.ae.tools.mcp
scripts/     setup, deploy, install-aegp, download-cep, enable-debug
```

## Conventions
- There are no feature panels. New capability goes in as an op: `vocabulary.js` + `describeOp` + `applyOne` in `engine.jsx`.
- The panel and the server both talk to the bridge through `shared/bridge-client.js`. Keep that file plain CommonJS/ES5-ish so it loads in CEP's Node.
- The bridge only calls AE APIs on the main thread (the idle hook). The network thread may call only `AEGP_CauseIdleRoutinesToBeCalled`.
- After changing bridge code, run `npm run test-bridge` before `npm run install-aegp`.
